{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793313856,"nonce":"7r/AupCsrnEwY+XpsnhluZacF5I=","title":"Preserve document identities and recovered drafts across file moves","message":"Parent authority track: 529764c1f9d8a4aa4fd6b9b203165dd4df383e332f1a4cbf110441de29bcaec2\nSession epic: ae3a156433377383faa317d5da1f34e6eab10f9a6e0d0ab0456fc0e0277a8382\nSafety prerequisite: e21511c98e97f403fbf661953c7359b0c20fb6767b7a738b4aa8435d3b50dc65\n\nIntroduce stable document IDs distinct from paths, private native state keys, compute generations and browser replicas. Carry IDs through native and hosted opens, selected recovery heads, browser recovery/undo/history and filesystem move events. Move file/directory bindings transactionally, preserving a released unsaved graph over its saved disk baseline without forcing Save. Closed clients and resumed replicas must resolve the same authorized identity after a move; an old path recreated as another file must never inherit its predecessor's graph or offline edits. Canonical aliases and case-only renames must not create competing owners.\n\nDefine and test an interruption-safe binding transition with source/destination and generation fencing. Deletion and explicit recovered-draft discard need intentional retirement/tombstones, acknowledgements, retention and recovery export rather than silent graph deletion or revival. Validate live/closed peers, offline edits, directory moves, destination collisions, failed/interrupted filesystem steps, alias retargeting, process restart and cross-host materialization. Preserve per-author undo, selected saved-versus-dirty heads and account/workspace isolation.\n\nThe current safety milestone refuses destructive mutations of released unsaved drafts and upgrades old private buffer bindings on reopen. It does not implement the identity/move protocol. Full filesystem/Git baselines, external-writer reconciliation and compute leases remain separate prerequisites before enabling automatic cross-host restore.","files":null}]}